WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:04.680
the version of Donald Trump that I call Downar.

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:11.549
Trump showed up yesterday in the Rose Garden
to sign an executive order about police departments

00:00:11.549 --> 00:00:15.129
directing police departments to stop using
chokeholds.

00:00:15.129 --> 00:00:19.030
And Donald Trump did look very, very unwell.

00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:21.279
And he said things that made no sense whatsoever.

00:00:21.279 --> 00:00:26.420
So this, again, raised questions about whether
Donald Trump is suffering the side effects

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:31.859
of some illness, side effects of medication,
cognitive decline, something else that we

00:00:31.859 --> 00:00:33.580
can't seem to put a finger on.

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:39.220
We discussed yesterday on the bonus show extensively
the question of police using chokeholds and

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:43.140
the reality that the priority should be rather
than a list of tactics that police can and

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:44.140
can't use.

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:48.660
The focus should be on training officers to
de-escalate situations so that chokeholds

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:50.310
aren't even in the picture.

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:51.930
But we talked about that yesterday.

00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:56.180
Right now, I want to focus on the absolute
implosion of Donald Trump during this Rose

00:00:56.180 --> 00:00:57.680
Garden statement.

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:01.610
Here is Donald Trump saying that we have developed
a vaccine for AIDS.

00:01:01.610 --> 00:01:03.170
Now, that's not true.

00:01:03.170 --> 00:01:07.950
We have not developed a vaccine for AIDS and
Trump, when he says it gets that look on his

00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:13.729
face where he seems to understand that he
said something wrong.

00:01:13.729 --> 00:01:16.710
But he almost is lost and doesn't know what
he said.

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:21.280
It was like that time where he did the oranges
of the investigation thing and he kind of

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:23.460
tries to back it up and mumbles a few things.

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:24.659
Take a look at this.

00:01:24.659 --> 00:01:31.159
They have come up with things and they've
come up with many other cures and therapeutics

00:01:31.159 --> 00:01:32.159
over the years.

00:01:32.159 --> 00:01:36.200
These are the people, the best, the smartest,
the most brilliant anywhere.

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:42.659
And they've come up with the AIDS vaccine
they've come up with or the AIDS.

00:01:42.659 --> 00:01:47.120
And as you know, there's various things and
now various companies are involved.

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:50.320
But the therapeutic for AIDS.

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:52.409
AIDS was a death sentence.

00:01:52.409 --> 00:01:57.740
And now people live a life with a pill.

00:01:57.740 --> 00:01:59.100
It's an incredible thing.

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:01.119
The Ebola vaccine.

00:02:01.119 --> 00:02:06.829
So that same confusion happened when Trump
repeatedly said he wanted to find out the

00:02:06.829 --> 00:02:10.479
oranges, the citrus fruit of an investigation.

00:02:10.479 --> 00:02:15.080
He said it twice and he had a look where he
knew he was saying something that didn't make

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:16.080
sense.

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:19.250
But he almost couldn't even pass it in his
own mind.

00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:21.670
It didn't get any better during the same event.

00:02:21.670 --> 00:02:23.730
Donald Trump seemed to lose his train of thought.

00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:26.730
This is another pattern we've seen where he
forgets what he's talking about.

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:29.540
He will just look at someone and say, right.

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:31.170
You know what I'm talking about, don't you?

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:32.510
We've seen this before.

00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:35.660
This time he looks into the audience and he
says right to him.

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:37.610
We're going to pursue things very strongly.

00:02:37.610 --> 00:02:42.760
You can tell if you're watching that Trump
doesn't seem lucid when you look at his face

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:44.200
right when this is happening.

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:45.220
Take a look.

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:52.590
And I gave a commitment to all of those families
today with Senator Tim Scott, Attorney General

00:02:52.590 --> 00:02:54.220
Bill Barr.

00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:58.420
We are going to pursue what we said.

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:01.670
We will be pursuing it and we will be pursuing
it strongly.

00:03:01.670 --> 00:03:02.670
Tim.

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:07.880
Mike Pence, wacky stuff at another moment.

00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:14.520
Donald Trump was talking about putting down
the protesters by using the National Guard.

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:21.530
And, of course, putting down is certainly
not the most humane language to use.

00:03:21.530 --> 00:03:27.750
Trump bragging about how strongly the protesters
were handled at your federal government is

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:37.030
ready, willing and able to help, as we did
in Minneapolis after he got out of control

00:03:37.030 --> 00:03:40.350
for four days.

00:03:40.350 --> 00:03:47.870
He sent in representatives commonly known
as the National Guard, and it was all put

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:49.270
down very quickly.

00:03:49.270 --> 00:03:50.520
We're willing to help.

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:53.580
We're willing to help in Seattle.

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:54.590
We're willing to help.

00:03:54.590 --> 00:03:55.830
Anywhere you want.

00:03:55.830 --> 00:04:02.480
So when there are protests against police
brutality and your response is to brag about

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:08.790
how much force you directed to be used against
the protesters, something is not quite getting

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:10.110
through.

00:04:10.110 --> 00:04:17.750
Then Donald Trump absolutely bizarrely interjecting
a complete non sequitur about school choice

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:19.749
being the civil rights issue of our time.

00:04:19.749 --> 00:04:21.049
Take a look at this.

00:04:21.049 --> 00:04:29.530
We're fighting for school choice, which really
is the civil rights of all time in this country.

00:04:29.530 --> 00:04:34.080
Frankly, school choice is the civil rights
statement of the year.

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:38.719
So understand that when Republicans talk about
school choice, what they really mean is defund

00:04:38.719 --> 00:04:43.749
public schools, weaken public schools, often
with voucher programs which go to charter

00:04:43.749 --> 00:04:48.740
schools, which then continues the vicious
cycle of worsening public schools because

00:04:48.740 --> 00:04:50.050
you've just pulled money from them.

00:04:50.050 --> 00:04:53.870
This is a favorite of Republicans say public
education is bad.

00:04:53.870 --> 00:04:55.650
Of course, it's underfunded.

00:04:55.650 --> 00:05:00.069
Use that to justify taking more money out
of public education, which makes it worse.

00:05:00.069 --> 00:05:02.220
So that then they can again justify.

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:04.080
Look at how bad public education is.

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:06.270
We've got to do more charter schools and private
schools.

00:05:06.270 --> 00:05:08.900
It's an old trope from Republicans.

00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:12.770
And then lastly here, another one of these
moments where Donald Trump lists different

00:05:12.770 --> 00:05:18.539
races and ethnicities and incorrectly claims
that almost everybody had a high paying job

00:05:18.539 --> 00:05:20.219
before the Corona virus hit.

00:05:20.219 --> 00:05:30.550
That's for almost every group, including black,
Hispanic, Asian women, young people, old people,

00:05:30.550 --> 00:05:34.710
young people without a high school diploma.

00:05:34.710 --> 00:05:37.629
Every group, everybody was thrilled.

00:05:37.629 --> 00:05:40.289
Everybody had.

00:05:40.289 --> 00:05:43.840
Just about high paying jobs.

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:48.110
Our country was never in a better position
and we were planning on massive growth.

00:05:48.110 --> 00:05:49.110
It was happening.

00:05:49.110 --> 00:05:50.360
It was already there.

00:05:50.360 --> 00:05:56.499
So one of the things we've seen in terms of
job creation before Corona coronavirus hit

00:05:56.499 --> 00:06:01.629
was that while the jobs numbers were good
and I have no problem admitting that a lot

00:06:01.629 --> 00:06:08.030
of the jobs being created where we're what
we call B.S. jobs, not medium or high wage

00:06:08.030 --> 00:06:12.249
jobs, but low wage jobs or sometimes jobs
that aren't even really jobs.

00:06:12.249 --> 00:06:14.870
They're contractor positions.

00:06:14.870 --> 00:06:18.560
And this is a common deception that we are
hearing from the right.

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:25.300
So there it is, a combination of Donald Trump
looking and sounding confused, making verifiably

00:06:25.300 --> 00:06:26.650
false claims.

00:06:26.650 --> 00:06:34.199
And the mood in the audience, a combination
of quiet confusion, horror, but also blind

00:06:34.199 --> 00:06:35.199
loyalty.

00:06:35.199 --> 00:06:39.240
The people that see this and at least tell
themselves that everything is completely fine.

